---------------------------------------------------------------------------
The example designs are not ours
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`examples/basic` holds hardware published by other people, included so the tool
can be tried against real designs rather than something written to suit it. The
MIT licence above covers this project's own code and does not extend to them.

  Adafruit INA3221 Breakout        (c) Adafruit Industries
  https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit-INA3221-Breakout-PCB

  SparkFun Thing Plus ESP32-S3     (c) SparkFun Electronics
  https://github.com/sparkfun/SparkFun_Thing_Plus_ESP32-S3

Both vendors publish their hardware as open source, Adafruit under CC BY-SA and
SparkFun under CC BY-SA 4.0 at the time of writing. Check the terms in the
repositories above before reusing either design; anything the tool writes from
them carries their terms with it, not this one.
